Step 4 (Wave D): 5 invoked agents + Agent 27 calibration lookup

Wave D contains 16 conceptual agents (25-40) but only 5 run per-upload at
runtime. The other 11 are research-only deliverables (orchestration,
prompt engineering, UX layouts, override capture, replay engine, cost
engineering, privacy posture, anti-overfitting discipline, red-team
synthesis) — schemas exist in shared/schemas.ts for completeness; no
invocation functions needed.

agent-25 Disqualifier Catalog (Opus, 600 tokens, VETO YES)
- Owns V1, V5, V7, V8, V9, V11. Defers V2/V3/V4/V6/V10 to owner agents.
- 11-veto registry; intentionally short list to avoid no-trade-machine
  drift.
- Calibration warning: 1/11 corpus rate is NOT production rate.

agent-26 Confirmation Bias Detector (Opus, 600 tokens, no veto)
- Red-teams every TAKE NOW candidate. Wave E section 4 consumes
  skepticism_score as [0.7, 1.0] multiplier on composite.
- Mandatory strongest_counter_argument + chart_evidence (or null).
- Asymmetric loss accounting: false-TAKE costs ~2x false-SKIP.
- Optional upstreamSummary input lets Wave E feed in current verdict
  context to make the red-team specific.

agent-28 Position Sizing & Tier (Sonnet, 500 tokens)
- V1 collapsed to GO/NO-GO + SMALL/NORMAL bucket per fixed 3-contract
  sizing. LARGE bucket gated until replay-engine validation passes
  (Agent 35 section 4).
- Pattern shape detection (single/pyramid_concentrated/staggered_reentry/
  cross_tier_cascade) per Image 09/10/11 exemplars.
- Cascade-add discount: -1 bucket per add depth.
- Behavioral state override: Agent 23 confirmed_tilt forces SMALL/SKIP.

agent-38 Robustness / Input Quality Gate (Sonnet, 600 tokens)
- Runs in Wave 0 as the input-quality pre-check (per Wave E spec
  section 0). Folder is waveD for naming consistency, function is Wave 0.
- 12 ranked heuristics across 3 severity tiers (HARD ABSTAIN /
  DEGRADE+FLAG / SOFT WARN). Cumulative degradation budget = 2.0.
- Emits context_bundle (platform/theme/instrument/timeframe/
  staleness/candle_count/score_cap) for downstream agents.
- Distinguishes platform-native annotations (NinjaTrader Entry/Target
  arrows) from user-drawn annotations.

src/lib/calibration/lookup.ts — Agent 27 NON-LLM lookup
- Per Agent 27 deliverable: per-upload calibration is a database
  lookup, not an LLM call. Recalibration loop (batch refit) lives
  in replay-engine sidecar.
- 4-state ladder (none/uncalibrated/rough/provisional/calibrated)
  driven by reconciled trade count per cell.
- Cold-start probability: linear interpolation between [0.30, 0.65]
  with ±20pp wide CI until N>=20 fitted.
- V1 production stub: always returns cold-start values; Phase 1.5
  Stage 5 + production reconciliation will populate calibration_active.

Tests: 38 new tests across 5 invoked agents + calibration lookup,
covering enum exhaustiveness, schema validation failures, abstain
handling, optional-context inputs (Agent 26 upstreamSummary, Agent 28
compositeScore), V1-specific gating (LARGE bucket rejected, contract
count clamps).

289 vitest passing total (251 from Wave C + 38 new).
134 pytest still passing. TypeScript type-check clean.

Stage 4 sampling note: 450-chart pilot batch (150/150/150) when
runner gets built post-Step 6 halt. Batch-aware: --size N --batch-id NNN.
